<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Cat FAQ</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --bg: #0b1020;
      --panel: rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.88);
      --panel-border: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2);
      --text: #e5eefc;
      --muted: #a8b3c7;
      --accent: #7dd3fc;
      --accent-strong: #38bdf8;
      --shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(2, 6, 23, 0.45);
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.12), transparent 32%),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #111827 0%, var(--bg) 100%);
      color: var(--text);
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      padding: 32px 16px;
    }

    .page {
      width: min(760px, 100%);
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
      border-radius: 24px;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .hero {
      padding: 40px 28px 20px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.16);
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
      line-height: 1.05;
    }

    .hero p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      max-width: 56ch;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .faq {
      padding: 20px;
    }

    .example + .example {
      margin-top: 14px;
    }

    .example {
      border: 1px solid rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.15);
      border-radius: 18px;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.86), rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.94));
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .question {
      width: 100%;
      border: 0;
      background: transparent;
      color: inherit;
      font: inherit;
      text-align: left;
      padding: 20px 22px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 16px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .question:hover,
    .question:focus-visible {
      background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08);
      outline: none;
    }

    .question-text {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }

    .icon {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      width: 18px;
      height: 18px;
      position: relative;
      color: var(--accent);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }

    .icon::before,
    .icon::after {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      left: 50%;
      top: 50%;
      width: 18px;
      height: 2px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: currentColor;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    }

    .icon::after {
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(90deg);
    }

    .question[aria-expanded="true"] .icon {
      transform: rotate(45deg);
    }

    .details {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-rows: 0fr;
      transition: grid-template-rows 0.25s ease;
    }

    .details[hidden] {
      display: none;
    }

    .details.is-open {
      grid-template-rows: 1fr;
    }

    .details-inner {
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .details p {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0 22px 22px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .hero {
        padding: 32px 22px 18px;
      }

      .faq {
        padding: 16px;
      }

      .question,
      .details p {
        padding-left: 18px;
        padding-right: 18px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="page">
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cat care guide</p>
      <h1>Frequently asked questions about cats</h1>
      <p>Quick answers for curious cat people, from sleep habits and scratching to hydration and social behavior.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="faq" aria-label="Cat frequently asked questions">
      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-1">
          <span class="question-text">Why do cats sleep so much?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="faq-1" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Cats are natural predators that conserve energy between short bursts of activity. Many cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day, and kittens or seniors often rest even more.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">
          <span class="question-text">Why does my cat knead blankets or my lap?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="faq-2" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Kneading is usually a comfort behavior that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats often knead when they feel safe, relaxed, and especially content in a favorite resting spot.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">
          <span class="question-text">How can I stop my cat from scratching the furniture?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="faq-3" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Offer sturdy scratching posts near the spots your cat already uses, reward them for choosing the post, and make furniture less appealing with covers or safe deterrents. Scratching is normal, so redirection works better than punishment.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">
          <span class="question-text">Do cats need a lot of water if they mostly eat dry food?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="faq-4" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>Yes. Cats on dry food often need extra encouragement to drink because they get less moisture from meals. Fresh water, multiple bowls, or a pet fountain can help support healthy hydration.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5">
          <span class="question-text">Why does my cat slowly blink at me?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="faq-5" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>A slow blink is often a sign of trust and calm. Many people think of it as a cat’s friendly signal, and gently blinking back can be a reassuring way to interact.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

    questions.forEach((button) => {
      const details = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));

        if (isExpanded) {
          details.classList.remove("is-open");
          details.hidden = true;
        } else {
          details.hidden = false;
          requestAnimationFrame(() => {
            details.classList.add("is-open");
          });
        }
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
